Package: driftd
Title: Easy Diffusion Model Fitting and Model Checks via 'rtdists'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jeremy", "Strueder", , "jstrueder@iese.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Eric-Jan", "Wagenmakers", role = "dtc",
           comment = "speed_acc data (Wagenmakers et al., 2008)"),
    person("Henrik", "Singmann", role = "dtc",
           comment = "speed_acc data as prepared in the rtdists package")
  )
Description: A wrapper around the 'rtdists' package (Singmann, Brown, Gretton, &
    Heathcote) that makes it easier to fit the diffusion decision model (Ratcliff &
    McKoon, 2008, <doi:10.1162/neco.2008.12-06-420>) to response time data and to
    analyze the results. All diffusion model densities, distribution functions and
    random numbers are computed by 'rtdists', which builds on the 'fast-dm' code of
    Voss and Voss. 'driftd' builds the likelihood from a model specification (which
    parameters vary across which conditions), fits it to each participant by maximum
    likelihood, and provides standard errors, analysis-ready parameter tables, model
    fit checks that compare observed and predicted response probabilities and response
    time quantiles with prediction intervals, model comparison, parameter and model
    recovery, and simulation from the fitted model.
